# Warning text

Explain a significant consequence before the person commits to an action.

## When to use

Use a short warning where an action can cause a meaningful loss or change that is easy to overlook. Place it before the decision. State the consequence and the affected object in plain language.

Do not use warnings for routine information, successful actions or every unavailable sensor. Repeated warnings lose their usefulness. A device safety interlock remains the responsibility of the device and integration; a styled warning is not an interlock.

